    "title": "<p>Terminology of clinical-genetic conditions relevant to clonal haematopoiesis</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Joseph David Khoury",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 708.7pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"945\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.45pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Condition</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 540.25pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"720\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Description</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clonal haematopoiesis (CH)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 540.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"720\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clonal outgrowth of haematopoietic cells from affected stem or progenitor cells, regardless of cause or disease state</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Age-related clonal haematopoiesis (ARCH)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 540.25pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"720\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CH detectable in blood or bone marrow and associated with ageing without a diagnosed haematological disorder or cytopenia; does not refer to specific gene alterations or quantitative criteria reflecting clonal abundance</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clonal haematopoiesis of indeterminate potential (CHIP)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 540.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"720\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CH with somatic mutations of myeloid malignancy&ndash;associated genes detected in the blood or bone marrow present at a variant allele frequency of &ge;&nbsp;2% in individuals without a diagnosed haematological disorder or unexplained cytopenia</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clonal cytopenia of undetermined significance (CCUS)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 540.25pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"720\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CH detected in the presence of one or more persistent cytopenias that are otherwise unexplained by haematological or non-haematological conditions and that do not meet diagnostic criteria for defined myeloid neoplasms</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.45pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Idiopathic cytopenia of unknown significance (ICUS)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 540.25pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"720\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Sustained and unexplained cytopenia without detectable blood cancer&ndash;associated driver mutations</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
